; @react-three/fiber 9.7.0 declares `react: >=19 <19.3` and this project is on
; React 19.3 — the range is simply behind upstream, not a real incompatibility
; (the 3D view runs fine on 19.3). Without this, a plain `npm install` fails with
; ERESOLVE. Strict peer checking would also drag the optional expo/react-native
; peers into the tree, which this browser-only app has no use for.
legacy-peer-deps=true
